		{
			"id": "pageAbout",
			"type": "page",
			"label": "About",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "textAbout",
					"type": "text",
					"text": "SAAM - Document Analysis - Execute Batch OCR Process step\n==========\n\nThe \"SAAM - Document Analysis - Execute Batch OCR Process\" custom steps enables an easy integration with the SAS Document Analysis (SDA) model, to run a full batch job, without the need to write any code.\n\nThe following OCR engines are supported: \n  * PaddleOCR (local)\n  * Microsoft OCR\n  * AWS Textract\n\nThe location of the generated output will be displayed for after running this step.\n",
					"visible": ""
				},
				{
					"id": "sectionPrereqs",
					"type": "section",
					"label": "Pre-requisites",
					"open": false,
					"visible": "",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "textPrereqs",
							"type": "text",
							"text": "A license for SAS Document Analysis (SDA) is required and you will need to know the name of the launcher context that was created during the deployment of SDA.\n\nPre-requisites:  Tested on Viya version Stable 2024.08 & Stable 2026.01",
							"visible": ""
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "sectionDocumentation",
					"type": "section",
					"label": "Documentation",
					"open": false,
					"visible": "",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "textDocumentation",
							"type": "text",
							"text": "* SAS Document Analysis documentation (https://go.documentation.sas.com/doc/en/aaimdacdc/default/aaimdawlcm/home.htm)",
							"visible": ""
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "sectionChangelog",
					"type": "section",
					"label": "Changelog",
					"open": true,
					"visible": "",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "textChangelog",
							"type": "text",
							"text": "* Version 1.11 (13OCT2026)\n     - Show the AI-generated content disclaimer at the top of the Options page, for every OCR engine\n\n* Version 1.10 (21AUG2026)\n     - Add optional setting to assign a deterministic batch output folder name:\n        - Generates a prefixed, timestamped name and passes it to the batch as BATCH_OUTPUT_FOLDER_NAME\n        - Reports the resulting batch output directory in the results\n        - Retains _sda_batch_output_folder_name and _sda_batch_output_directory for downstream steps\n\n* Version 1.9 (28MAY2026)\n     - Renamed step from \"OCR - Document Analysis - Execute Batch OCR Process\" to \"SAAM - Document Analysis - Execute Batch OCR Process\" to conform to the SAAM naming standard\n\n* Version 1.8 (22APR2026)\n     - Add the following options and associated defaults:\n        - Retain line breaks (True)\n        - Generate images from PDFs (False)\n        - Output mapping file format (XSLX)\n\n* Version 1.7 (22APR2026)\n     - Remove \"bypass SSL\" option. Default to False\n\n* Version 1.6 (16APR2026)\n     - Communicate exit codes for failed SDA batch processes\n\n* Version 1.5 (19FEB2026)\n     - Use absolute path for python command\n\n* Version 1.4 (09OCT2025)\n     - Add PaddleOCR to OCR engine options\n     - Add MS OCR model name - available when \"Microsoft\" is selected as the OCR engine\n     - Add Custom Document Intelligence model name - available when \"Custom\" is selected as the MS OCR model\n     - Remove optional setting to maintain directory structure\n\n* Version 1.3 (25FEB2025)\n - Use launcher context name instead ID\n\n* Version 1.2 (04NOV2024)\n     - Added option to wait for batch completion with ability to specify a max wait time.\n\n* Version 1.1 (09OCT2024)\n     - Implemented feedback\n\n* Version: 1.0 (07OCT2024)\n      - Initial version",
							"visible": ""
						}
					]
				}
			]
		}
